RG DS OS: a 64 MiB CMA region instead of BananaLinux's 256 MiB

RG DS OS has no vendor display stack: the direct present's scanout buffers are a few MiB of CMA, and the GPU
(panfrost) allocates from system memory. The smaller region saves about 60 ms of boot (its setup took 88 ms) and
leaves 192 MiB to the games.

--- a/rk356x-base.dtsi	2026-10-27 18:00:00
+++ b/rk356x-base.dtsi	2026-10-27 18:00:00
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@
         linux,cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reusable;
-			size = <0x0 0x10000000>;
+			size = <0x0 0x4000000>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
